st_accel: the LIS3DSH, the iPad mini 1's accelerometer.

The ADT's arm-io/i2c2/accelerometer (compatible "accelerometer,ap3dsh",
address 0x1d) answers WHO_AM_I with 0x3f: an ST LIS3DSH, which st_accel does
not know.  It is the LSM330's accelerometer on its own -- the same registers
(ODR, BDU and the axes in 0x20, the range in 0x24, the data-ready interrupt
in 0x23) -- so its entry is a copy of the LSM330's with its WHO_AM_I, and
with ODR value 0x07 as 400 Hz, not 200: measured on the iPad by the FIFO's
fill (0x06: 5 samples in 60 ms, 0x07: 22, 0x08: full), as the LIS3DSH's
datasheet has it.

    git diff -- drivers/iio/accel/

diff --git a/drivers/iio/accel/Kconfig b/drivers/iio/accel/Kconfig
index 8c3f7cf55..979259b39 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/accel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/iio/accel/Kconfig
@@ -418,7 +418,7 @@ config IIO_ST_ACCEL_3AXIS
 	  Say yes here to build support for STMicroelectronics accelerometers:
 	  LSM303C, LSM303DLH, LSM303DLHC, LIS3DH, LSM330D, LSM330DL, LSM330DLC,
 	  LIS331DLH, LSM303DL, LSM303DLM, LSM330, LIS2DH12, H3LIS331DL,
-	  LNG2DM, LIS3DE, LIS2DE12, LIS2HH12
+	  LNG2DM, LIS3DE, LIS2DE12, LIS2HH12, LIS3DSH
 
 	  Also need to enable at least one of I2C and SPI interface drivers
 	  below.
